<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41090" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-murmŭro</span></b> ,
			āre, v. a. and n.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to murmur
			back</i>, <i>remurmur</i> (<b>poet.</b>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">remurmurat unda,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 10, 291</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pinus remurmurat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 5, 1, 153</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">carmina remurmurat echo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Calp.
					Ecl. 4, 28</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to murmur back</i>,
				<i>object</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si quis quid remurmurat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Front. Ep. ad Amic. 2, 6</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
